style="width:30%; border-radius:10px; margin:0px 0px 10px 15px; float:right;">

<p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:bold; margin-top:0;">
REAL-WORLD CONNECTION: When AI Invented Court Cases
</p>

<p style="font-size:16px;">
In 2023, two lawyers used ChatGPT while preparing documents for a real court case. The AI generated legal cases and citations looked professional and convincing.
</p>

<p style="font-size:16px;">
The problem? Several of the cases did not actually exist.
</p>

<p style="font-size:16px;">
The lawyers submitted the fake citations to the court and were later fined $5,000. The judge explained that while AI can assist with professional work, humans are still responsible for checking whether information is accurate.
</p>

<p style="font-size:16px; margin-bottom:0;">
This case became an early public example of how AI systems can sound extremely confident, even when the information they generate is completely wrong.
</p>
<br>

<p style="font-size:14px; margin-bottom:0;">
<b>Note</b>: This case study is included as part of the Warm-Up Activity in <a href="https://studio.code.org/courses/ai-discoveries-2026/units/1/lessons/7" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lesson 7: Verifying AI Output</a>.
</p>


</div>
